{"base_rate":0.3039647577092511,"brier":0.09608678414096918,"bss":0.5458396716198862,"bss_hi":0.620962032276088,"bss_lo":0.4444817373882823,"chart":{"base":[324.8,94.9],"fp":[310.6,333.9],"lead":"62,194.5 272,177.1 482,156.9 692,114.5","note":{"base":"skill 0.55 — higher than 96% of cities","fp":"low end +6pp, high end +1pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.7 °C — better than 11% of cities","rel":"promised 1% → rained 5%; promised 93% → rained 91%"},"rel":"65.3,444.7 244.7,273.3 651,71.8"},"country":"MA","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.06412628487518358,"ess":252.9747447157206,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Tangier</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Tangier rain forecast is strongly skilful, though 4 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (99%), believe about\n<b>95%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(1%), there is still roughly a <b>5%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 681 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-03-26. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 11.5 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.55, ranked 9 of\n216 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(4&ndash;39) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>1%</td><td class='num'><b>5%</b></td><td class='num'>405</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>15%</td><td class='num'><b>32%</b></td><td class='num'>68</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>43%</td><td class='num'><b>56%</b></td><td class='num'>71</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>85%</td><td class='num'><b>86%</b></td><td class='num'>58</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>99%</td><td class='num'><b>95%</b></td><td class='num'>79</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">4 of 5 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Tangier</b> <span class=\"muted\">Morocco</span></p>\n  <div class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Strongly skilful</span><details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What does this label mean?\" title=\"What does this label mean?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>Compared with a simple guess: saying &ldquo;30% chance of rain&rdquo; every day, because it rains here on 30% of days.</p><p>The forecast did far better.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details>\n    <span class=\"muted\">4 points off by more than chance</span></div>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score<details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What is the skill score?\" title=\"What is the skill score?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>How much better the forecast is than that simple guess. 0 means no better, 1 means perfect, below 0 means worse. Day-ahead rain forecasts usually score 0.3 to 0.5.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details></dt><dd>0.55</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>4&ndash;39\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 216</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>681 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Tangier &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Tangier\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"59.82681481481482,377.5061728395062 109.43411764705881,296.3529411764706 209.7214084507042,187.1830985915493 360.18172413793104,43.10344827586209 410.11797468354433,18.0 410.11797468354433,27.215189873417728 360.18172413793104,105.86206896551727 209.7214084507042,264.0845070422535 109.43411764705881,355.2352941176471 59.82681481481482,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"271.3568281938326\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"271.3568281938326\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"59.82681481481482,364.0246913580247 109.43411764705881,264.2352941176471 209.7214084507042,176.92957746478874 360.18172413793104,68.20689655172418 410.11797468354433,36.430379746835456\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 1%&amp;#10;It rained 5% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 405 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"59.82681481481482\" cy=\"364.0246913580247\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 15%&amp;#10;It rained 32% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 68 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"109.43411764705881\" cy=\"264.2352941176471\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 43%&amp;#10;It rained 56% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 71 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"209.7214084507042\" cy=\"176.92957746478874\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 85%&amp;#10;It rained 86% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 58 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"360.18172413793104\" cy=\"68.20689655172418\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 99%&amp;#10;It rained 95% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 79 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"410.11797468354433\" cy=\"36.430379746835456\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(30%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Tangier the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>spring</b> (0.52) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (0.18).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>7%</td><td class='num'>0.177</td><td class='num'>3.5%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>179</td><td class='num'>28%</td><td class='num'>0.502</td><td class='num'>5.7%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>175</td><td class='num'>51%</td><td class='num'>0.506</td><td class='num'>11.1%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>147</td><td class='num'>37%</td><td class='num'>0.522</td><td class='num'>6.1%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":35.76727,"lon":-5.79975,"n":681,"n_cities":216,"name":"Tangier","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.08,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.005160493827160493,"n":405,"obs":0.04938271604938271,"sig":true},{"hi":0.28,"lo":0.08,"mean":0.1452941176470588,"n":68,"obs":0.3235294117647059,"sig":true},{"hi":0.7,"lo":0.28,"mean":0.42859154929577453,"n":71,"obs":0.5633802816901409,"sig":true},{"hi":0.98,"lo":0.7,"mean":0.8536206896551725,"n":58,"obs":0.8620689655172413,"sig":false},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.98,"mean":0.9946835443037976,"n":79,"obs":0.9493670886075949,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":11.5,"provisional":false,"rank":9,"rank_hi":39.0,"rank_lo":4.0,"reliability":0.0064736160062919094,"resolution":0.1204490274934413,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"tangier","station":"","timezone":"Africa/Casablanca"}